Patches applied to the deps/libdb submodule before building it.

Named libdb-<pinned tag>-<topic>.patch, applied with "cd deps/libdb &&
patch -p1" idempotently by deps/build_libdb.sh.  Drop a patch when the
pin moves past the upstream commit that carries the same fix.

## Current patches (pin v2026.10.5 = 553b649a1)

Four libdb defects dbsql found and fixed; source-only here (the matching
regression tests live in the libdb tree and in .agent/libdb-bugs/tests/,
and the full git-format-patch set with those tests is in
.agent/libdb-bugs/patches/).  See .agent/libdb-bugs/README.md for the
analysis of each.

- libdb-v2026.10.5-r7-txn-remevent-abort-leak.patch
    R7.  __txn_doevents freed a child txn's TXN_REMOVE event only on
    commit; on abort it leaked.  src/txn/txn_util.c.
- libdb-v2026.10.5-r9-recover-foreign-file.patch
    R9.  Recovery meeting a referenced file that is now foreign/empty
    (EINVAL) failed all of recovery and panicked (abort, under
    DIAGNOSTIC).  Treat EINVAL like the already-tolerated ENOENT.
    src/dbreg/dbreg_util.c, src/dbreg/dbreg_rec.c.
- libdb-v2026.10.5-r10-log-emfile-nopanic.patch
    R10.  __log_name panicked the environment on any non-ENOENT open
    error; EMFILE/ENFILE are transient and are now returned to the
    caller.  src/log/log_put.c.
- libdb-v2026.10.5-r11-compact-move-metadata-handle-lock.patch
    R11.  __db_move_metadata took the moved-page handle lock under the
    dbp's own handle locker while inside a txn that already WRITE-held it
    from a sibling dbremove, self-deadlocking compaction.  Acquire under
    the txn locker instead.  src/db/db_compact.c.

## History

The libtool FreeBSD host-pattern fix this directory carried for
v2026.10.1/.2 (freebsd1* matching FreeBSD 10-19, so no shared library
was built) is upstream as of libdb v2026.10.3 (6e1f1c86a).

Note: in v2026.10.3+ five build_windows/*.sln/*.vcproj files are stored
with CRLF line endings against .gitattributes' "* text=auto", so
"git status" in the submodule lists them as modified on a fresh
checkout.  Cosmetic; the build does not use them.
